             "const resultValue=(v,fallback)=>{v=assertResultI64(v);return v[0]?v[1]:assertI64(fallback());};"
             "const resultError=(v,fallback)=>{v=assertResultI64(v);return v[0]?assertI64(fallback()):v[1];};"
             "const sameType=(a,b)=>a===b||(Array.isArray(a)&&Array.isArray(b)&&a.length===b.length&&a.every((x,i)=>sameType(x,b[i])));"
             ;; P3 of superproject adr-2609242100: a typed value is walked in
             ;; full ONCE, at a trust boundary (an exported function's
             ;; parameters, a capability result), by an explicit-stack
             ;; iterative walk against a traversal budget -- `budget/boundary-
             ;; nodes` / `budget/boundary-bytes` (lang/limits.edn
             ;; :language/boundary). Inside the module a constructor checks only
             ;; its own node and the tags of its immediate operands
             ;; (`shallowTyped`), and an internal call only the tag
             ;; (`assertOperand`). There is no depth or node limit on a value.
